@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+# MINDS: changes from the released code (cspjiao/MINDS @ ce9fac0, AAAI 2024)
+
+## G-repro (released `run.py`, Christianity, unchanged)
+- Hits@100 0.576 at the best epoch, against the paper's 0.6250 (Table 2): −7.9% relative. **Pass.**
+- The released loop selects the epoch by test MAP@100.
+- Log: `../minds_repro_christianity.log`.
+
+## Benchmark adapter (`minds_bench.py`)
+1. **Hypergraphs from training cascades only.** The released `run.py:201` builds them from all cascades, validation and test included.
+2. **Selection on validation.** The released micro criterion (MAP@100) is computed on 2,000 validation cascades, with the released patience of 10. The released code selected on test.
+3. **Previous-user mask built on the GPU.** It is element-wise identical to the released `get_previous_user_mask`, which builds it on the CPU.
+4. **Data.**
+   - Benchmark splits; cascades truncated to their first 500 events. The released loader drops cascades longer than 500.
+   - Social graph from edges created before the validation window, as an undirected `dhg.Graph`, as released.
+5. **Dependencies.** `dhg==0.9.4` and `optuna` live in `../pydeps_dhg`. Packages the environment already has were moved to `../pydeps_dhg_shadowed`, so they do not shadow it.
+
+**2026-10-27 fix.** The final training loop hard-coded batch 64; only the probe read `BATCH`. It now uses `BATCH` (default 64, unchanged), and validation uses min(64, `BATCH`).
+- **Unaffected:** all earlier runs used the default.
+- **Affected:** the Telegram one-epoch runs, which had silently trained at 64 instead of the probed batch.
+
+**2026-11-08, `SCORE_ONLY=1` (leakage test).** Skips training and scores the checkpoint already in OUT, loaded onto DEVICE (`map_location`). Used by the leakage test (`opb leakage`) to score one checkpoint on the original and the cut world. Released results are unaffected.
+
+- **Tuning check (2026-11-13; paper, Appendix F.3).** Environment overrides of the hyperparameters listed there; when unset, every value equals the released run.
